// B35, and it was the only one of the family that the two compilers DISAGREED about — stage-0
// refused it and stage-1 accepted it, which is worse than a shared leak. A shared leak is
// invisible to the differential because both sides answer the same wrong thing; a disagreement is
// exactly what the differential exists to catch, and it could not, because no fixture spelled it.
//
// No pattern, no `dynamic`, no relay function. A plain `let`, and then a field READ of it:
// `expr_allocates` had no arm for a field access or an index, so the taint on `b` was thrown away
// the moment anything reached through it. Proven: printed `ab`, then `0` after a clobbering region.
//
// It also bounded B27 — taint reached a `for` binding correctly and the field read discarded it —
// and it was found by the agent that had already measured its own fix green, by probing shapes the
// 133-program corpus did not cover.
class Box { name: String }
class Holder { tag: String }
let mutable h: Holder = Holder { tag: "start" };
region r {
    let b: Box = Box { name: "a" + "b" };
    h.tag = b.name;
}
print(h.tag);
region clobber {
    let mutable k: Int = 0;
    while k < 40 { let junk: String = "ZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ" + to_string(k); k = k + 1; }
}
print(h.tag);
